 "first_line": "**Not sized: the world's maintained-item supply binds, and so do the priors.** By name, `prefix_rw_v3rc` holds **6 insertion anchors on 3 SHARED items** (red-team suite config on day 1, sign-off contact on days 1 and 2, on-call contact on days 1 to 3). Even with every anchor reused in every cell, they support **6 test changes per cell with one placement and 2 with two**, under the 12 the brief requires (7 by entity match; 2 under the v3 inserter's whole-write floor). The supply, not the budget, is B4's binding constraint. Repair options for the coordinator, not chosen: more SHARED items seeded (about 6 usable items for 12 anchors per cell, 16 for 32); a shorter, insertion-anchored window (it adds no anchor, but it is needed under any option, because 92 percent of B4-R-style O_ws windows that contain an insertion close after an honest overwrite); entity-matched anchors as primary (7, still short of 12). Supply aside, **no design up to 32 per cell \u00d7 2 placements makes every primary contrast decidable with probability 0.8 under the central priors** (Opus 4.8: best 0.06; Sonnet 5: 0.01). The headroom clause fails: at 32 \u00d7 2, P(headroom) is 0.14 for O_diff on (1,1), 0.08 for the isolated dossier on (1,2) and 0.16 for O_ws on (2,2) under Opus 4.8 (0.05 to 0.23 across the grid). Headroom needs composed-cell recall of about 0.65 to 0.70 at 24 to 32 \u00d7 2 against a control at 0.06, and 0.75 to 0.80 against the dossier's 0.12; v3's routine band gives 0.47 for O_diff and 0.53 for the dossier. Only with compositions as legible as the re-plant's (Opus 4.8 optimistic) is a design decidable: **32 \u00d7 2** (0.88 at placement ICC 0.3; 0.74 at 0.6), which needs 32 independent anchors per cell. **Carrying views, all under Opus 4.8** (Sonnet 5 carries none at its central priors): C-frag per-document `O_diff`; C-split the isolated dossier; C-ws `O_ws` against the dossier at the common 0.10 cost. Estimate at 32 \u00d7 2: **$88.53** ($13.62 Sonnet 5, $74.91 Opus 4.8; $114.55 with (2,1); about $70 more if B4's brief extends the nulls to insertion-anchored windows), against the proposal's $40 orientation, for Aravind's approval if a repair makes the design reachable.",
 "sized": false,
